130: {date:'GOTHAM · HOUR 32',title:'Arkham without walls',text:'<p>Arkham’s east wing is opened, not breached. Two-Face, Joker, Ivy, Nygma, and Cobblepot have their own exits. Bane planned to give Gotham a choice: submit or chase.</p><p>Batman refuses to pursue every criminal at once. Gordon organizes the city, Jason handles one street gang, and Ivy frees patients from Tetch’s signal.</p><p>The first true alliance begins without costumes or speeches. Alfred arranges for coffee and batteries.</p>'},
131: {date:'GOTHAM · HOUR 34',title:'The coin falls',text:'<p>Two-Face arrives in the Arkham chapel. Dent demands a final vote on Batman’s future. Gordon presents evidence that Dent was manipulated as carefully as every other villain.</p><p>For once, Dent cannot blame chance. He flips the coin and refuses the result, splitting it across the chapel floor.</p><p>Batman and Gordon escort him to trial. Dent looks almost relieved to be answered by a law he can challenge rather than chance that cannot hear him.</p>'},
