133: {date:'GOTHAM · HOUR 38',title:'The silent promise',text:'<p>Joker has rigged Wayne Manor’s cave elevator with a trap. Batman enters believing Alfred is trapped inside. Instead Alfred is still at the manor, guiding a civilian evacuation.</p><p>The Joker appears on every monitor. “No mask,” he says, “no miracle.” Batman answers in Bruce Wayne’s voice: there is no miracle, only a team that can survive the next minute.</p><p>Joker loses interest in a man who cannot be reduced to a single reaction. He escapes toward Bane’s citadel.</p>'},
134: {date:'GOTHAM · HOUR 39',title:'The last enemy',text:'<p>Bane offers Batman the city in exchange for surrendering the Batcave. All Gotham must do is kneel, Bane says, and he will stop breaking it.</p><p>Batman refuses. Alfred, Gordon, Jason, Fox, Croc, Ivy, Dent, and the Penguin’s former workers link into a plan spanning streets, towers, tunnels, and servers.</p><p>Bane calls them a crowd. Batman calls them Gotham.</p>'},
135: {date:'GOTHAM · HOUR 40',title:'Forty hours until dawn',text:'<p>At the end of forty hours, Batman faces Bane above the flooded central square. He does not win because he is stronger. He wins because preparation has turned every lesson into a choice.</p><p>Jason prevents a collapse. Gordon opens the escape routes. Ivy disables the venom pumps. Croc removes Bane’s final supports. Dent and Cobblepot choose their own codes of justice. Joker, Nygma, and Tetch are confined where they cannot direct the city.</p><p>Dawn reaches Wayne Tower. Bruce watches with Alfred and knows the promise is not to end fear. It is to keep working until every frightened person can come home.</p><p class="quote">The first night became forty hours. Gotham remained. So did the work.</p>'},
