  Line 147: {date:'WAYNE CAVE · BEFORE DAWN',title:'The first lesson',text:'<p>Alfred lays the self-defense field guide on the workbench. It is not as impressive as the suit, the car, or the glowing computer screens. Its pages are worn at the corners, full of diagrams and notes in Alfred’s neat hand. Bruce opens it carefully.</p><p>“Begin with the book,” Alfred tells him. “Learn how to keep your balance. Learn when to move, when to listen, and when walking away is the bravest thing you can do.” Bruce looks toward the equipment waiting around the cave. For the first time, it feels less like a collection of answers and more like a list of responsibilities.</p><p>There is still a long way to go. But the work has finally begun.</p>'},

  Line 154: {date:'GOTHAM · HOUR 08',title:'Killer Croc below',text:'<p>During a subway evacuation, Killer Croc overturns a construction train. Batman finds the panic is real but the attack is scripted: the train carries stolen medical serum for Bane.</p><p>Croc could have escaped. Instead he remains to protect trapped maintenance workers. Batman recognizes manipulation, but not enough to release Croc without judgment.</p><p>Alfred extracts the workers. Croc disappears below the city, leaving a warning: “He knows where you sleep.”</p>'},

