  Line 169: {date:'WAYNE CAVE · THE PLAN TAKES SHAPE',title:'Tools, not answers',text:'<p>They work in fits and starts. Alfred knows how to keep a project moving; Bruce knows how to ask questions that make the project bigger. The computer station becomes a place to sort reports and maps. A suit bay takes shape against the stone. The elevator connects the cave to the estate without sending either man through the front hall.</p><p>Every object has a purpose and a limit. Batarangs can distract or disarm, but they cannot make a bad decision wise. Smoke pellets can cover a retreat, but they cannot turn a retreat into a victory. A grapple prototype can bridge a gap only if the person using it thinks before leaping.</p><p>Bruce begins to see the cave not as a lair, but as a workshop for learning how to help.</p>'},

  Line 171: {date:'WAYNE CAVE · BEFORE DAWN',title:'The first lesson',text:'<p>Alfred lays the self-defense field guide on the workbench. It is not as impressive as the suit, the car, or the glowing computer screens. Its pages are worn at the corners, full of diagrams and notes in Alfred’s neat hand. Bruce opens it carefully.</p><p>“Begin with the book,” Alfred tells him. “Learn how to keep your balance. Learn when to move, when to listen, and when walking away is the bravest thing you can do.” Bruce looks toward the equipment waiting around the cave. For the first time, it feels less like a collection of answers and more like a list of responsibilities.</p><p>There is still a long way to go. But the work has finally begun.</p>'},

  Line 172: {date:'GOTHAM · HOUR 01',title:'The first patrol',text:'<p>At 02:14, Bruce leaves the cave in the unfinished suit. The city is wet, violent, and divided into islands of light. Alfred watches on the radio, correcting course without pretending to know the way.</p><p>Bruce stops a mugging near Crime Alley. The victim asks why a masked man would help. Bruce answers that the city was not enough to save his parents, then recognizes that this is not the whole truth.</p><p>He returns before dawn. Alfred: “You survived. Tomorrow, we improve the plan.”</p>'},

