197: {date:'GOTHAM · HOUR 40',title:'Forty hours until dawn',text:'<p>At the end of forty hours, Batman faces Bane above the flooded central square. He does not win because he is stronger. He wins because preparation has turned every lesson into a choice.</p><p>Jason prevents a collapse. Gordon opens the escape routes. Ivy disables the venom pumps. Croc removes Bane’s final supports. Dent and Cobblepot choose their own codes of justice. Joker, Nygma, and Tetch are confined where they cannot direct the city.</p><p>Dawn reaches Wayne Tower. Bruce watches with Alfred and knows the promise is not to end fear. It is to keep working until every frightened person can come home.</p><p class="quote">The first night became forty hours. Gotham remained. So did the work.</p>'},
